## What

Adds a new **"Sandbox, no internet"** preset (`sandbox-no-internet`) to the `managedSettings` endpoint of the mock-policy-server (`scripts/mock-policy-server/endpoints.ts`).

The preset serves this managed-settings body:

```json
{
  "sandbox": {
    "enabled": true,
    "allowBypass": true,
    "userPolicy": {
      "network": {
        "allowOutbound": false
      }
    }
  }
}
```

## Why

Makes it easy to exercise the "sandbox enabled, but no outbound network" managed-settings policy path against the local mock server: the agent runtime sandbox is turned on (with bypass allowed) while outbound network access is denied, so sandboxed tools run offline.

## Notes for reviewers

- Placed among the existing security/permission presets (right after `lockdown-allowlist`).
- The GUI preset dropdown is populated dynamically from this definition (`renderPresets` in `public/app.ts`), so no other files (HTML, docs, tests) needed changes.
- Verified the file loads via `node --experimental-strip-types` (the same mechanism the server uses), the serialized body matches exactly, and all `managedSettings` preset IDs remain unique.
- The endpoint has `schema: true`, but that check is only a non-blocking "keys not in schema" GUI hint; `sandbox` is a legitimate runtime-owned managed setting.

When the Agents Window is running in screen reader optimized mode, the usual VS Code status bar indicator is unavailable because this window does not include a status bar.

Add a visible **Screen Reader Optimized** badge immediately to the right of the command center. The badge should:

- react to changes in screen reader optimized mode;
- use localized text and theme-aware styling;
- remain non-interactive and accessible without adding duplicate announcements;
- participate in the title bar overflow behavior.
